LIFELINK SOS – A Predictive Self-Healing Offline Emergency Communication Network for Reliable Emergency Message Delivery

1. Introduction

Life Link SOS is an IoT-based emergency assistance and safety system designed to support wireless communication and real-time monitoring. The system uses ESP8266 NodeMCU and LoRa communication technology to transmit and receive data over long distances.

2. Abstract

Life Link SOS aims to provide a reliable wireless communication system for emergency assistance. It uses LoRa technology to transmit data from the transmitter to the receiver. The ESP8266 NodeMCU receives the transmitted information and displays the data through an LCD and a web-based dashboard. The dashboard provides real-time monitoring of received packets, signal strength, temperature, and humidity. This system demonstrates the use of IoT and wireless communication for safety and monitoring applications.

3. Objectives

- To develop a wireless emergency communication system.
- To implement long-range communication using LoRa technology.
- To monitor transmitted and received data.
- To display information through an LCD.
- To develop a web-based monitoring dashboard.
- To improve communication reliability during emergency situations.

4. Hardware Requirements

